## Review Rules

### Automatic Review Requests

- All PRs will automatically request review from:
  - Global owners for major changes
  - Directory-specific owners for targeted changes
  - Security team for authentication/authorization changes

### Review Requirements

- **Security Changes**: Must be approved by @frontal/security-team
- **Breaking Changes**: Must be approved by @frontal/core-team
- **Documentation Changes**: Must be approved by @frontal/docs-team
- **Workflow Changes**: Must be approved by @frontal/devops-team

### Review Escalation

If owners are unresponsive after 3 business days:
1. Tag @frontal/core-team for escalation
2. Create issue in project board for tracking
3. Consider alternative approvers from global owners list

## Approval Requirements

### Required Approvers

| Change Type | Required Approvers | Minimum Reviews |
|--------------|-------------------|-----------------|
| Security | @frontal/security-team | 2 |
| Breaking Changes | @frontal/core-team | 2 |
| New Features | Directory owners | 1 |
| Bug Fixes | Directory owners | 1 |
| Documentation | @frontal/docs-team | 1 |
| Infrastructure | @frontal/devops-team | 1 |

### Merge Requirements

- All automated checks must pass
- Required approvals must be received
- No merge conflicts
- PR must be open for at least 24 hours (except for urgent fixes)

## Emergency Changes

For critical security fixes or production issues:

1. Create PR with "emergency" label
2. Immediate review from @frontal/core-team
3. Can merge after single approval from core team
4. Must create follow-up issue for post-mortem

